     7	This is descriptive only, with no arm and no GPU. The question was written before tallying: do the arm-2 empty mechanisms (7 call-exhaustion never-edited, 3 malformed `edit_file`) recur on v012? Decision rule, fixed before tallying: if fewer than 3 of 33 v012 rows are non-timeout empties attributable to edit failure or call exhaustion, a tool-level lever has too few target rows to beat ±3 noise on 33. In that case I propose shelving it rather than spending an arm.
     8	
     9	## 3. What I did
    10	- Read the harness code. `edit_file`, `get_status` and the budget warning are fixed harness code that a bundle cannot change. The harness attaches an automatic `budget_warning` once 10 or fewer **calls** remain (`swegemma/tools/base.py:47-63`). There is **no automatic time warning**, but the agent can query one: `get_status` (`swegemma/tools/execution.py:119`) reports remaining time, elapsed agent time and remaining calls. The one tool path a bundle controls is a skill script: `run_skill_script` runs `python3` in the sandbox work dir (`adk_eval_core/sandbox/base.py:164+`), so a tolerant-edit helper is technically possible. Using it would still need prompt text, so the bundle would need its own score (dec 087).
