    23	Files: `results/plan011_diag_arm3_main.json`, `results/plan011_diag_arm3_smoke.json`. Classifier inputs: `results/plan009_arm3_{main,smoke}_d4cdf0f0.json`. The 18 empty-timeout rows (main + smoke) used a median of 15.5 tool calls (range 5–41). In 7 of them the agent made 10 or fewer calls in the whole 210 s, which points to the clock running out during model generation rather than calls running out. Overlap: 1 row (41 calls, `get_status` at call 41 showed 40 used / 0 remaining / ~18 s left) had already used up its calls before the timeout. The classifier's precedence still labels it `empty_timeout`, but it counts as call exhaustion too; with it, the rule's tally is 1 < 3. That is the thinking-4096 time sink plan 010 targets. Script review: `ops/codex/review-20261107T121430.md`. Its three BLOCKING items were all about report text: (1) median/≤10 counts used main-only data, now fixed to all 18; (2) call-exhaustion overlap, now acknowledged; (3) `get_status` time signal, now described. The table counts were independently reproduced. Non-blocking issues (whitespace-vs-zero-byte empty predicate, the `empty_edit_failed` label not checking response success, and inventory validation) have zero effect on these rows. They are recorded for any reuse, which will use the exact-byte predicate and inventory checks.
